# normative-is-theorem.rule — the RFC-001 §6 materialization (Jena RETE rule).
#
# Every NormativeStatement that is not itself an axiom is a Theorem: a claim that
# must be grounded (its premises chase back to axioms). Applied via rdf_reason
# over //corpus:corpus_standards, this types the 19 SEC NAV claims (and the ratio
# corpus claims) as :Theorem, so the grounding check can ask "does every
# assertion derive from axioms?" The regulatory root claims are marked
# :isAxiom true and stay axioms (excluded by the noValue guard).

@prefix rfc: <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/rfc#>.
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>.
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>.

[normative-is-theorem:
    (?s rdf:type rfc:NormativeStatement)
    noValue(?s rfc:isAxiom 'true'^^xsd:boolean)
    ->
    (?s rdf:type rfc:Theorem)
]
